@page "/"

<PageTitle>Witcher 2 Save Editor</PageTitle>

<h1>The Witcher 2 Save Editor</h1>

<p class="lead">
    A multiplatform save game editor for The Witcher 2: Assassins of Kings.
</p>

<div class="card mt-4">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h5 class="card-title">Getting Started</h5>
        <p class="card-text">
            Navigate to the <a href="editor">Editor</a> page to upload and edit your Witcher 2 save files (.sav).
        </p>
        <h6>Features:</h6>
        <ul>
            <li>Load and parse <code>.sav</code> files (DZIP/LZF compressed format)</li>
            <li>Browse all save data sections (quests, facts, world state, etc.)</li>
            <li>Edit values (integers, floats, booleans, strings)</li>
            <li>Export modified save files</li>
            <li>View the full save data tree structure</li>
        </ul>
        <h6>Save File Sections:</h6>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>saveInfo</strong> &ndash; Save metadata, difficulty, save message</li>
            <li><strong>questSystem</strong> &ndash; Active quests and quest states</li>
            <li><strong>questLogBlock</strong> &ndash; Quest log progress</li>
            <li><strong>facts</strong> &ndash; World facts and story flags</li>
            <li><strong>worldInfo</strong> &ndash; Current world/location data</li>
            <li><strong>dynamicEntities</strong> &ndash; NPCs, items, entities in the world</li>
            <li><strong>playerSpawn</strong> &ndash; Player position and spawn info</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>
